<div class="mw-heading mw-heading2"><h2 id="Controversy">Controversy</h2><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=The_Bachelor_(American_TV_series)_season_27&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10" title="Edit section: Controversy"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<p>Contestant Greer Blitzer faced controversy shortly after the season premiere after tweets of her defending <a href="/wiki/Blackface" title="Blackface">blackface</a> were uncovered, <a href="/wiki/The_Bachelor_and_race" title="The Bachelor and race">continuing the trend</a> of contestants with racist social media histories being cast in the franchise.<sup id="cite&#95;ref-61" class="reference"><a href="#cite_note-61"><span class="cite-bracket">&#91;</span>58<span class="cite-bracket">&#93;</span></a></sup> On January 24, 2023, Blitzer issued an apology for her past behavior.<sup id="cite&#95;ref-62" class="reference"><a href="#cite_note-62"><span class="cite-bracket">&#91;</span>59<span class="cite-bracket">&#93;</span></a></sup> 
</p><p>The incident was further addressed during the <i>Women Tell All</i> special on March 14, 2023, with host <a href="/wiki/Jesse_Palmer" title="Jesse Palmer">Jesse Palmer</a> acknowledging the franchise's failings to adequately address serious topics such as racism in the past.<sup id="cite&#95;ref-63" class="reference"><a href="#cite_note-63"><span class="cite-bracket">&#91;</span>60<span class="cite-bracket">&#93;</span></a></sup> Blitzer also confirmed that she was educating herself on the history of blackface and had met with Dr. Kira Banks, a psychologist and diversity consultant.<sup id="cite&#95;ref-64" class="reference"><a href="#cite_note-64"><span class="cite-bracket">&#91;</span>61<span class="cite-bracket">&#93;</span></a></sup>
</p>
